Hi,
attached is a patch against netbsd-5 which allows to build alpha with
X11FLAVOUR=xorg. I didn't test clients yet (but I don't expect issues here).
scanpci runs fine. xorg -configure completes and gives a sensible
xorg.conf, with the right driver, and the right PCI ID. But I couldn't
get a working graphical display yet. with a Permedia graphic (compaq-suplied
adapter) and glint driver, the server loops waiting for a adapter's
register getting the right value.
With a TGA 3d30 adapter, the server just do nothing, and the gray X11 screnn
doesn't appear. The tga driver prints suspicious values to the xorg log
(all 0xff) which I assumes it gets from the adapter's registers, so it's
possible reading adapter registers don't always works the way it should.

Now I did these tests with a XP1000; there may be issues specific with this
platform, because a know-working netbsd-3 XFree86 binary, which is in use on
a PWS500 with the same netbsd-5 kernel, doens't work on the XP1000.
I'll do more tests with a PWS500 this evening. 
Does anyone know of differences between the PWS500 and the XP1000 which
could explain X not working on the XP1000 (even with a know-working-on-PWS500
X server), and how to fix it ?
Also, I did a hack in xf86sym.c to get things build (in?/out? is a #define
on NetBSD/alpha, and so SYMFUNC() doesn't work); could someone familiar
with alpha and/or xorg infrastructure tell me if this can cause problems ?

-- 
Manuel Bouyer <bouyer@antioche.eu.org>
     NetBSD: 26 ans d'experience feront toujours la difference
--

--BXVAT5kNtrzKuDFl
