On macppc they're memory writes with a barrier, on sparc64 we don't =20
need the barrier.

>> If that's not the case please ignore the bit about =20
>> PCI_MAGIC_IO_RANGE.
>> For mga you won't need PIO anyway.
>
> thanks !

Years ago I wrote a hack to let xfree86 access generic, otherwise =20
unsupported PCI graphics controllers through a slightly abused /dev/=20
fb* ( the last remnant of that is in machfb ) - I had an U10 running =20
XFree86 with four heads, the onboard Rage Pro, a Creator3D, a =20
Millennium I and a Millennium II ( both with PC firmware so X had to =20
do all the legwork ) - it didn't support PCI IO space at all yet the =20
Matrox cards just worked fine, with some minor endiannes-related =20
glitches As far as I know the only non-x86 firmware you can get for =20
these cards is Apple-specific, so the driver writers probably used =20
#ifdef __powerpc__ all over the place.

If you use VGA text mode you may want to allow X to use the vgahw =20
module which does need PCI IO space access in order to mess with the =20
resp. vga registers.

have fun
Michael

